WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.917 --> 00:00:02.875
Kid 1: Whoa.

00:00:02.875 --> 00:00:05.042
Did you know that so much
plastic is drifting out in

00:00:05.042 --> 00:00:07.708
the ocean that it has
made a giant island?

00:00:07.708 --> 00:00:10.042
Two times the size of Texas!

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:14.125
You think I could, like, make a
resort on it...hey, what’s that?

00:00:14.125 --> 00:00:17.000
Kid 2: It’s this old video
game system that dad insisted

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.500
made him a “hardcore gamer”.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.000
I’m pretty sure it
just makes him old.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.208
Kid 1: What’s it called?

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:25.583
Kid 2: Super Mallio Brothers.

00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:28.000
Hey, it’s not working!

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.500
Kid 1: Precise electronic
that would surely fry if the

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.500
slightest bit of
liquid meets it?

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.750
Try blowing on it.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.000
Kid 2: That logic seems sound.

00:00:48.458 --> 00:00:50.375
Mallio: Ok LuiVC.

00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:53.708
Let’s go save the Princess.

00:00:53.708 --> 00:00:55.750
Oh mamma mia

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:59.458
Princess, you’re
supposed to start in the castle.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:01.042
Polly Mer: Not this time Mallio.

00:01:01.042 --> 00:01:03.167
Now I’m leading the adventure.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:07.125
LuiVC, that demotes you from
sidekick to third wheel.

00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:10.167
LuiVC: Ohh, Mamma Mia.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:12.125
LuiVC lose!

00:01:12.125 --> 00:01:13.333
Polly Mer: Stop it.

00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:15.000
We have bigger concerns.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.417
Bisphenowser is up
to no good again.

00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:18.125
Mallio: Oh no.

00:01:18.125 --> 00:01:20.000
What is he doing now?

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.625
Polly Mer: He’s decided to
build himself a new castle,

00:01:22.625 --> 00:01:26.458
made entirely out of plastic,
without any concern about what

00:01:26.458 --> 00:01:28.667
that will do to
the environment.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.375
You know how he does it.

00:01:30.375 --> 00:01:34.292
Tons of hard plastic spikes,
molten plastic moats,

00:01:34.292 --> 00:01:37.250
go-kart track, all that stuff.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.625
Mallio: But how does using
plastic hurt the environment?

00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:44.167
Polly Mer: Wait, don’t you guys
know anything about plastic?

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:47.208
LuiVC: Ummm...When you
grab it, you become

00:01:47.208 --> 00:01:49.333
invincible for a short time?

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:51.750
Polly Mer: Nope,
that’s the stars.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:52.458
LuiVC: Oh.

00:01:52.458 --> 00:01:53.875
Then no.

00:01:53.875 --> 00:01:55.250
Polly Mer: Of course not.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.042
What did I expect from
two guys who constantly

00:01:58.042 --> 00:01:59.833
hit bricks with their heads?

00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:02.083
Anyway, you guys need
to know everything about

00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:04.500
plastic to defeat Bisphenowser.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.458
Let’s start at Bisphenowser’s
plastic factory.

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:13.792
LuiVC: Hey, what are they doing?

00:02:13.792 --> 00:02:15.792
Polly Mer: That’s
how plastic is made.

00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:19.125
Fossil fuels such as crude
oil and natural gas are heated,

00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:23.125
causing them to break down into
small molecules called monomers.

00:02:28.292 --> 00:02:30.208
These monomers can
be combined to form

00:02:30.208 --> 00:02:32.542
long chains called polymers.

00:02:32.542 --> 00:02:34.750
And these polymers are plastics!

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:43.500
LuiVC: But I thought
that fossil fuels are used

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.375
to produce energy?

00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:46.958
Polly Mer: That’s also right.

00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:50.708
Even this factory runs on
energy from fossil fuels, and

00:02:50.708 --> 00:02:53.708
all this use of fossil
fuels greatly contributes to

00:02:53.708 --> 00:02:55.917
pollution in our environment!

00:02:55.917 --> 00:02:59.417
Mallio: LuiVC, we’ve
got to stop this!

00:03:06.083 --> 00:03:07.542
Polly Mer: Good job.

00:03:07.542 --> 00:03:09.042
Lets go now.

00:03:10.458 --> 00:03:13.125
LuiVC: Aaahhh! What’s
with all the stink clouds?

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:16.250
Polly Mer: That’s all dioxin
Boollution, and with everything

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:20.375
Bisphenowser has been doing,
it’s getting really bad.

00:03:20.375 --> 00:03:22.167
LuiVC: Dioxin boolution?

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:23.583
What’s that?

00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:26.625
Polly Mer: Dioxins are highly
toxic chemicals released into

00:03:26.625 --> 00:03:29.042
the atmosphere during the
production of the plastic

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:32.917
polyvinylchloride,
also known as PVC.

00:03:32.917 --> 00:03:35.792
Dioxins can cause
many health problems.

00:03:35.792 --> 00:03:37.292
Mallio: Let’s
get out of here.

00:03:37.292 --> 00:03:39.667
I think that I would
rather fight Bisphenowser

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.708
than breathe in this Boolution.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:50.083
LuiVC: Whoa, that’s
a lot of plastic.

00:03:50.083 --> 00:03:52.208
What is it all doing here?

00:03:52.208 --> 00:03:54.125
Polly Mer: This must be
where Bisphenowser is

00:03:54.125 --> 00:03:56.542
disposing of his plastic waste.

00:03:56.542 --> 00:03:59.333
Mallio: You mean he’s just
gonna leave it out here?

00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:01.500
Polly Mer: Most likely, yes.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.500
Many commonly used plastics are
not biodegradable, meaning that

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.500
they don’t break down over time.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.417
Instead, they are going
to stay here forever.

00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:13.208
LuiVC: What are those
mushrooms doing?

00:04:13.208 --> 00:04:16.250
Polly Mer: Bacteria and fungi,
such as those mushrooms,

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:19.917
are decomposers, meaning that
they can break down matter.

00:04:19.917 --> 00:04:23.792
Some fungi and bacteria, not
that particular mushroom, can

00:04:23.792 --> 00:04:27.875
even decompose a small amount
of some types of plastics–

00:04:27.875 --> 00:04:29.583
but it’s not enough.

00:04:29.583 --> 00:04:32.208
Mallio: So mushrooms
are really helpful?

00:04:32.208 --> 00:04:34.542
Polly Mer: Yes, and thats
why you guys should stop

00:04:34.542 --> 00:04:36.042
eating so many of them.

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:38.500
Mallio: Well at least
plastics can’t do any harm

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.083
by just sitting out here

00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:42.458
Polly Mer: Actually, they can.

00:04:42.458 --> 00:04:46.000
Toxic chemicals can accidentally
leak out of the plastics and

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.000
into the landfills and
eventually into the groundwater.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.333
LuiVC: But what’s
toxic in plastic?

00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:55.083
Polly Mer: Chemicals
like BPA and phthalates.

00:04:55.083 --> 00:04:58.917
BPA is used to make clear
polycarbonate plastics and

00:04:58.917 --> 00:05:02.667
epoxy plastics that coat
the inside of food cans.

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:06.625
BPA is an endocrine-disruptor,
meaning that it can interfere

00:05:06.625 --> 00:05:08.667
with the hormones in our body.

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:11.833
And phthalates are chemicals
added to plastics to improve

00:05:11.833 --> 00:05:14.000
flexibility and durability.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.208
Like BPA, Some phthalates
can also cause problems to

00:05:17.208 --> 00:05:20.792
the endocrine system, while
others can cause cancer.

00:05:20.792 --> 00:05:23.875
Once these chemicals enter the
ground water, they can be easily

00:05:23.875 --> 00:05:26.417
absorbed by plants,
and they can also

00:05:26.417 --> 00:05:28.958
enter rivers, lakes, and oceans.

00:05:28.958 --> 00:05:30.292
Come on, I'll show you.

00:05:36.417 --> 00:05:39.042
LuiVC: What’s wrong with
those purple animals?

00:05:39.042 --> 00:05:41.250
Polly Mer: These animals have
been getting their water and

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.083
food from this BPA
contaminated pond,

00:05:44.083 --> 00:05:46.417
just downhill from the landfill.

00:05:46.417 --> 00:05:49.458
Just like in humans, BPA
contamination will cause

00:05:49.458 --> 00:05:52.333
reproductive problems
in plants and animals.

00:05:52.333 --> 00:05:55.000
And this gets worse
higher up the food chain.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:59.208
First, small organisms called
plankton absorb tiny amounts of

00:05:59.208 --> 00:06:01.083
the toxins from the water.

00:06:01.083 --> 00:06:04.167
Then when fish eat hundreds
of these plankton, they absorb

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:05.875
the chemicals in each one.

00:06:05.875 --> 00:06:08.208
This magnification
process happens again

00:06:08.208 --> 00:06:10.375
when the animals eat these fish.

00:06:10.375 --> 00:06:13.708
Once in the organism, the toxin
is very hard to get rid of-

00:06:13.708 --> 00:06:17.042
so it just accumulates
inside the organism.

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:18.042
Mallio: Oh no!

00:06:18.042 --> 00:06:19.833
What should we do
about the landfill?

00:06:19.833 --> 00:06:22.250
LuiVC: We could
burn the plastic!

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.958
Polly Mer: Actually,
that’s a bad idea.

00:06:24.958 --> 00:06:28.167
Burning plastic greatly pollutes
the environment by releasing

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:30.708
toxic chemicals
into the atmosphere.

00:06:30.708 --> 00:06:34.125
Mallio: Well then, we better
go stop Bisphenowser.

00:06:38.417 --> 00:06:40.583
LuiVC: Oh no, they’re choking!

00:06:43.083 --> 00:06:45.792
Mallio: Look at
all this plastic.

00:06:45.792 --> 00:06:49.250
Polly Mer: Yes, many plastics,
especially plastic pellets,

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.125
often end up in oceans.

00:06:51.125 --> 00:06:54.875
These pellets are especially
harmful to fish, because they

00:06:54.875 --> 00:06:56.875
are easily mistaken for food.

00:06:56.875 --> 00:07:00.125
Once eaten, the pellets
block their digestive system

00:07:00.125 --> 00:07:01.292
and they die.

00:07:01.292 --> 00:07:03.417
Mallio: We’ve got to
defeat Bisphenowser.

00:07:06.583 --> 00:07:10.875
LuiVC: Hey, what’s
over there in the ocean?

00:07:10.875 --> 00:07:14.417
Mallio: It looks like a
floating pile of trash.

00:07:14.417 --> 00:07:16.792
Polly Mer: That's
actually all plastic.

00:07:16.792 --> 00:07:21.208
Every year, 8 million tons of
plastic is put into the ocean.

00:07:21.208 --> 00:07:24.625
That's equivalent to 5
plastic bags for every foot of

00:07:24.625 --> 00:07:25.958
coastline in the world.

00:07:28.083 --> 00:07:32.417
Bisphenowser: Who dares
enter my plastic kingdom?

00:07:32.417 --> 00:07:36.042
Mallio: Ehhh...
It’s-a-me, Mallio.

00:07:36.042 --> 00:07:38.000
LuiVC: And LuiVC!

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:42.917
Mallio: I feel like you
are borrowing this from

00:07:42.917 --> 00:07:44.042
someone else...

00:07:46.875 --> 00:07:50.542
Look at
Bisphenowser’s health bar!

00:07:50.542 --> 00:07:53.292
LuiVC: Oh! It looks like
Bisphenowser has been

00:07:53.292 --> 00:07:55.958
poisoned by all that plastic!

00:07:55.958 --> 00:07:59.750
Polly Mer: Bisphenowser probably
ingested the BPA, dioxins, and

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:03.417
phthalates that the plastic
released into the air and water.

00:08:07.708 --> 00:08:09.917
LuiVC: That did it!

00:08:09.917 --> 00:08:12.833
Polly Mer: Sure, but those
chemicals in the air, water, and

00:08:12.833 --> 00:08:15.292
ground will take
longer to get rid of.

00:08:15.292 --> 00:08:19.250
Even a small impact from plastic
pollution can cause a large

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:21.500
problem in the environment.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.208
Mallio: What can we do to help?

00:08:23.208 --> 00:08:26.292
Polly Mer: You should avoid
using plastic when possible.

00:08:26.292 --> 00:08:30.333
Bring a reusable grocery bag,
use your own takeout containers,

00:08:30.333 --> 00:08:32.917
and carry a reusable
bottle for drinks.

00:08:32.917 --> 00:08:36.042
LuiVC: And if you have
to use plastic, make sure

00:08:36.042 --> 00:08:37.875
you know where to recycle it.

00:08:37.875 --> 00:08:40.875
Polly Mer: Yup So what do
you guys want to do now?

00:08:40.875 --> 00:08:43.667
Mallio: Do you want
to play tennis?

00:08:43.667 --> 00:08:44.417
LuiVC: No

00:08:44.417 --> 00:08:46.250
Mallio: How about go-karts?

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.417
LuiVC: Nah

00:08:47.417 --> 00:08:49.708
Mallio: What about soccer?

00:08:49.708 --> 00:08:50.458
LuiVC: No

00:08:50.458 --> 00:08:52.958
LuiVC: Let’s
just throw a party!

